==In the manga==
[[File:Hidden Village EToP.png|thumb|250px|Hidden Village in [[The Electric Tale of Pikachu]]]]
===The Electric Tale of Pikachu===
The Hidden Village appeared in ''[[ET07|Pikachu's Excellent Adventure]]''. After meeting [[A.J.]] and [[Samurai]] and learning from them about the Hidden Village, where Pokémon abandoned by their Trainers supposedly lived under the protection of a "goddess", {{OBP|Ash Ketchum|EToP|Ash}}, {{an|Misty}}, and {{an|Brock}} left to search for it and boarded a bus. However, {{AP|Pikachu|Pikachu (EToP)}} was briefly distracted by talking to a {{p|Charmander}} and a {{p|Squirtle}} and was accidentally separated from Ash as a result. Pikachu, Charmander, and Squirtle left to search for the Hidden Village themselves, joined along the way by a wild boy named {{OBP|Tommy|EP034}} and his adoptive mother, {{p|Kangaskhan}}. When the group of travelers met the [[Team Rocket trio]], the trio decided to pretend to be helpful and joined the group in order to get to the Hidden Village themselves, hoping to steal rare Pokémon from there.

When the travelers eventually reached the Hidden Village, they were met by the village's protector, an ordinary girl named [[Melanie]], whom the local Pokémon viewed as a goddess due to her kindness. Team Rocket started attacking the Pokémon of the village to capture them, but were quickly sent flying by Kangaskhan's {{m|Mega Kick}}. While Charmander had a tearful reunion with its Trainer, [[Damian]], Pikachu left the village to go reunite with Ash.
